The streetlamps are already shining as I take Ludwig's leash.
We must go out for a short walk before bedtime.
He wags his tail happily, and we go out onto the pavement.
The air is cool tonight.
Ludwig sniffs at everything on the way.
Suddenly he stops by a trash can.
There is a dirty paper bag lying on the ground.
He sticks his snout right down to it.
I pull gently on the leash.
"No, Ludwig, leave it!" I say firmly.
He looks up at me, but tries again.
"Come here," I say and pull him a little away.
"You must not eat trash from the street."
Nina said that he may only eat his own dog food.
He looks disappointedly at the bag.
"We must go home now," I say and begin to walk.
He follows me, and I pet him.
"Good dog," I smile.
Now we just have to go home and sleep.
